## HOLDS (the standing lines; every 2026-10-27 line is carried)
- Signature classes pause for Kam: production, money, external communication to any human, anything irreversible. No box, no `az`, no deploy, no merge, no `--admin`. No Docker unless a queue item names it (none does).
- Comms are ticket comments only, BLUF-first, facts only, ONE per queued ticket at READY FOR GATE after its PR is up, on your queued tickets only. **No comment to or `@` mention of Peter or Stuart**; anything needing a human to act goes to Wednesday as an escalation candidate (Peter and Stuart are TOLD, never asked). You never change a ticket's state or assignee: the board seat does.
- **Search before filing anything** (by the symbol, file path or error string, never your own phrasing) with a positive control that fires AND a zero control. **Do not use `zzqqxx-no-such-symbol-9931` (burned) or `zzqz-wed-ctl-4417` (used by the drafter at 15:4x; it returned 0 then); coin a fresh token you have not written to the board and do not record it in a ticket.** A finding outside your tickets goes in the READY mail for Wednesday to file.
- Never delete (quarantine into a dated folder, record the move). No `--no-verify`, no force push; merge develop in, never rebase a pushed branch. One worktree per ticket; the shared checkout is untouched after boot. Never `cd`; absolute paths only.
- **Mail discipline:** every mail names `Seat Z <N>th` on body line 1 and starts its subject with `[Secuura/Blockchain-Z -> Wednesday]`. Never put stop, hold, checkpoint or hand over in a mail SUBJECT. Plan confirmation is mailed before any edit. One batch READY mail at the end. A QUESTION mail (Context, one Question, Meanwhile, Needed-by) only for a blocker; after ~15 minutes with no ANSWER proceed on the safest reading unless approval-class.
- **TWO HTML DOCS (STANDING_LINES 2026-10-27; repo skill `.claude/skills/secuura-test-discipline` section 4):** every PR that changes a test GRANTS you `Projects Documents/API_Security_Functional_Testing_Architecture_Flow_Diagrams.html` and `Projects Documents/QA_Tool_Cheat_Sheet_Secuura_API_Testing.html` (quote the path: the space in `Projects Documents`) for APPENDING that ticket's own entry in the shape of an existing one (e.g. KS-1364's), in the same commit. A PR that is comment-only or doc-only takes the skill's escape clause: say so in the PR with the reason. **Both docs are append-only for every seat on the floor and their SECTION NUMBER is set at MERGE time, never at commit time**: write your block with a placeholder number, tell Wednesday, and the merger renumbers to develop's highest + 1 (re-verify tags balanced, append-only, `html_docs_matrix.test.sh`). Several seats append in one wave: merge develop in before each push and keep both sides' entries.
- **PUSH WINDOW LOCK** (one pre-push at a time on this laptop). The lock is acquired ONLY by your own successful `mkdir`: `mkdir /Volumes/DevMASTER/!CODING/Secuura/Blockchain/worktrees/.push-lock`; set a flag INSIDE the poll loop on the `mkdir` that SUCCEEDED, proceed only on that flag, read stderr on a failure (EEXIST vs anything else) before saying "held by another seat", write `holder` (`Seat Z <N>th | pid | branch | start UTC ISO`) only if your mkdir created the dir. **Poll at 3 s or less, bounded.** With the lock held: `pgrep -fl '^/bin/sh [.]githooks/pre-push origin git@github[.]com:'` must print nothing (the anchored pattern is LOAD-BEARING: never simplify it, a suite fixture runs the same hook against a scratch origin) and `uptime` load1 < 16. Push with keepalives for THAT COMMAND ONLY: `GIT_SSH_COMMAND="$(git config --get core.sshCommand) -o ServerAliveInterval=15 -o ServerAliveCountMax=120" git push -u origin <branch> > out 2>&1; rc=$?` (rc on its own line), then `git ls-remote origin <branch>` in the same action. **RELEASE removes `holder` and THEN `rmdir`, rc on its own line; a failed release is a loud STOP, never a silent HELD=0.** Release only after the push rc and the ls-remote are in hand; release between branches. One timeout-shaped refusal is retried ONCE at load1 < 12; a second is a stop. Read `.githooks/pre-push` at your base and cite the line that allows each push.
- **A short private TMPDIR** (`/tmp/<seat-letter>`): `tsx` opens a unix socket under `$TMPDIR` and macOS caps the path near 104 bytes; a TMPDIR under the session scratchpad makes `generate-openapi`, any `tsx` script and socket-binding shell suites die `listen EINVAL` / 7-of-11, which reads like a repo defect. Say which TMPDIR you used in the evidence.
- **A gating read runs in its OWN call before the action it gates** (`ls-remote` before a push, `git diff --cached` before a commit, a sha256 check before a restore). Reverts are `git checkout <path>` plus a sha256 against HEAD, never a pattern you wrote. **A conflict RESOLVER reads the merge's own result first:** resolve only when the merge rc is 1 AND `MERGE_HEAD` exists AND `git diff --name-only --diff-filter=U` is non-empty; any other rc is a STOP.
- **Identity:** a worktree has no per-worktree config, so `git config user.*` inside one WRITES the shared checkout. Pass `git -c user.name='Kam Kreiser' -c user.email=kamil.kreiser@secuura.ai commit ...` and read it back from the commit (`git log -1 --format='%an <%ae>'`). Only a SCRATCH CLONE may `git config` locally.
- **A fresh worktree/clone has no gate and no shared build:** `npm ci --ignore-scripts`, then `npm run build --workspace=packages/shared` and assert `packages/shared/dist/index.js` (without it 76 api-gateway files fail on the environment alone), `core.hooksPath .githooks`, `test -x .githooks/pre-push`, `git config --get core.hooksPath` read back in the plan confirmation. For Prisma use `npm run generate --workspace=services/originate`.
- **Test-discipline instruments:** a mutant is applied to a COPY (sha256 before and after, restore proved against HEAD); a control that cannot fail is not a control (run each verifier against a known-bad subject); a "corrupted patch" control corrupts CONTENT, never a hunk start line; exit codes on their own line (`cmd > out 2>&1; rc=$?`), never through a pipe; no `timeout` on macOS; bash 3.2 syntax in shell; `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control beside every zero count; `grep -F` needs `-e` for a pattern starting with `-`. Linear NORMALISES markdown on store: compare copied BLOCKS, never whole descriptions.
- PR titles, bodies and commits carry only YOUR tickets' keys hyphenated; write any other as `KS 1555`-style (space, no hyphen). `Refs`, never `Closes`. The Test Evidence block in the PR body is yours, with ratios (`N/N ran`), never "all". **One PR per ticket** (a ticket's items ride one PR unless a QUEUE line says otherwise).
- **READY FOR GATE** = five things that EXIST and are named in the mail: the PR number, its head sha read from origin in the same action, the ticket comment naming the PR, the Test Evidence block in the PR body, and what was NOT done or NOT covered. You stop there; Wednesday commissions the gate and GOs each merge by head sha. Rotate inside your 80-90 band, handover first.
- **Shared inbox:** `secuura-blockchain@agentmail.to` is read by many seats at once. Act only on mail naming your own full seat name (`Seat Z <N>th`, ordinal included; an earlier occupant of letter Z is FOREIGN). A mail naming no seat is a QUESTION, not a guess. Arm a matcher that reads the other seats' subjects as FOREIGN and prove it on their real subjects.
- **Your first line names your pane id**; check `$TMUX_PANE` against it, never against a pane title.

